<P/>
<table style="background-color:#004400">
  <tr>
    <td colspan="2" style="color: white; text-align:center">
      &nbsp;&nbsp;Primary data source&nbsp;&nbsp;
    </td>
    <td style="color: white; text-align:center">
      Query NIST Bibliographic Database for <b>Ar  XVIII</b> (new window)
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
<!--    <td style="text-align:center; background-color:#DDDDBB">-->
    <td class='brt2'>
      &nbsp;<a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Ar XVIII';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19200&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Ar&amp;spectr_charge=18&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Shabaev&nbsp;2015</a>, <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Ar XVIII';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=3620&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Ar&amp;spectr_charge=18&amp;type=E');return false">Erickson&nbsp;1977</a>&nbsp;
    </td>
    <td class='blf2'>
      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The data refer to the isotope <sup>40</sup>Ar. Erickson's theoretical values of ionization energies were scaled to the <a target="_blank" href="https://physics.nist.gov/constants">CODATA-2018 values of the fundamental constants</a> and then subtracted from the ground-state ionization energy given by <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Ar XVIII';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19200&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Ar&amp;spectr_charge=18&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Shabaev&nbsp;2015 </a>. Additional corrections were applied to the <i>n</i>S levels, as described by <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Ar XVIII';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=12548&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Ar&amp;spectr_charge=18&amp;type=E');return false">Kramida&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2008 </a>. The <i>n</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;2 energy levels were taken directly from <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Ar XVIII';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19200&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Ar&amp;spectr_charge=18&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Shabaev&nbsp;2015 </a>. Their uncertainties are given for excitation energies from the ground state; for the rest of the levels, uncertainties are given for separations from the ionization limit. The present data set was prepared by A. Kramida (unpublished) for the release of ASD v. 5.10 in September 2022.
    </td>
    <td class='bcn2'>
      <A HREF="javascript:void(0)" ONCLICK="popbib('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/Elevbib/make_query.cgi?spectra=Ar%20XVIII&amp;method=EL&amp;method=TE&amp;method=ND&amp;method=IP&amp;method=SF&amp;method=QF&order=1');return false"
        ONMOUSEOVER="self.status='Ar  XVIII: bibliography energy levels query';return true;"
        ONMOUSEOUT="self.status=''; return true;" TARGET=_blank>Literature on Ar  XVIII Energy Levels</A>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
